=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data source (web useTranslation; the leaf is fed a `drive` prop by its parent):
    bound through the P1/S8 seam DriveScoreSource→DriveScoreModel. The web component is
    a pure presentational leaf, so the snapshot carries the SI drive (distance_m,
    duration_s, max_speed_mps, start/end_battery_pct) plus the parent's loading/error/
    connectivity state. No HTTP in the view.
  - Scoring (web computeDriveScore + getScoreColor): ported VERBATIM in
    DriveScoreScoring.compute — the 150 Wh/km optimal target, the 750 Wh-per-battery-%
    estimate, the four clamped components (efficiency 40 / speed 20 / range 20 / trip 20),
    and the Math.round rounding. getScoreColor → DriveScoreTone (<40 bad, <70 warning,
    else good). EXECUTED-green against hand-computed web values (40 km/40 min drive ⇒
    total 74; all-defaults drive ⇒ 23; harsh 2 km drive ⇒ 4 with clamped 0s).
    Inputs are SI and the surface renders only the unitless score, so NO unit-system
    conversion applies at any layer (matches the web source).
  - Composition (web GlassPanel + SVG ring gauge + breakdown bars):
      • GlassPanel  -> TSGlassPanel.
      • ring gauge  -> ZStack(background Circle stroke + tone-coloured trimmed arc +
                       centred score number + "Score" caption); arc + number animate in
                       (web motion.circle sweep), instant under Reduce Motion.
      • breakdown   -> 4 rows, each a label + value/max chip + proportional bar; colours
                       map web hex → brand tokens (efficiency #00f0ff→accent, speed
                       #a855f7→chartSeriesPower, range #10b981→chartSeriesBattery, trip
                       #f59e0b→chartSeriesEnergy); gauge tone bad→statusDanger #ef4444,
                       warning→statusWarning #f59e0b, good→statusSuccess #10b981.
      • layout      -> ViewThatFits(HStack | VStack) so it stacks under compact width /
                       large Dynamic Type instead of truncating.
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + a projection/model unit test):
      loading (skeleton ring + bar skeletons) · empty (no trip to score — distance &
      duration both ≤ 0 ⇒ friendly ContentUnavailableView, never a blank box) · error
      (message + Retry) · data (gauge + breakdown) · stale (freshness chip + "score may
      be stale" banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition) · offline (cached
      score kept + offline chip + "showing last known score" banner).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved verbatim — driveScore.title/score/efficiency/
    speedDiscipline/rangePreservation/tripLength; native chrome namespaced driveScore.*
    (live/stale/offline/refresh/staleBanner/offlineBanner/loadingA11y/empty/errorTitle/
    retry). referenced==declared VERIFIED: 16 keys referenced in Swift == 16 keys declared
    in DriveScore.strings, 0 on either side. NO English string literals in native code
    (all via DriveScoreStrings facade + Text(verbatim:)).
  - Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on the gauge ("Drive Score, {score}"), each breakdown
    row ("{label}, {value}/{max}"), the freshness chip, the refresh button, the retry
    button, and the banners; the panel is an accessibility container; Dynamic-Type system
    fonts (Font.TS); Reduce Motion honored (gauge arc + bar fills + TSFadeIn + TSSkeleton).
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): DriveScoreModel.start() emits view.opened with surface slug
    "DriveScore" exactly once (OSLogDriveScoreTelemetry default; prod app injects the
    shared diagnostics adapter). Asserted once-only by the model test.

